'''''Oenothera stricta''''', the '''fragrant evening primrose''' (a name it shares with other members of its genus), is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Onagraceae]].<ref name="RHS_96931" >{{cite web |title=''Oenothera stricta'' fragrant evening primrose |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/96931/oenothera-stricta/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=3 December 2023 |quote=Synonyms; ''Oenothera odorata'' misapplied ... 2 suppliers }}</ref> It is native to the [[Desventuradas Islands]], Chile, and southern Argentina, and it has been introduced to many locations around the world.<ref name="POWO_614101-1" >{{cite POWO |id=614101-1 |title=''Oenothera stricta'' Ledeb. ex Link |access-date=3 December 2023 }}</ref> The unimproved species is available from commercial suppliers, as is a cultivar, 'Sulphurea'.<ref name="RHS_96931" /><ref name="RHS_69658" >{{cite web |title=''Oenothera stricta'' 'Sulphurea' evening primrose 'Sulphurea' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/69658/oenothera-stricta-sulphurea/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=3 December 2023 |quote=Synonyms; ''Oenothera odorata'' 'Sulphurea', ''Oenothera odorata'' 'Cream' ... 9 suppliers }}</ref> The [[Royal Horticultural Society]] considers both to be good plants to attract pollinators.<ref name="RHS_96931" /><ref name="RHS_69658" />

==Subtaxa==
The following subspecies are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_614101-1" />
*''Oenothera stricta'' subsp. ''altissima'' {{small|W.Dietr.}} – southern Argentina
*''Oenothera stricta'' subsp. ''stricta'' – Desventuradas Islands, Chile, introduced worldwide
